#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078223 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d7a21aa-f2e3-5461-81a6-5cbd0f63c03d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Last Term and the Sum"}] :question/id #uuid "8d663147-d71b-5349-bb5b-c737d73d4d7e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4206" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is $S_{20}=560,$ and the last term is $a_{20}=66,$ what is the first term of the series?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}(a_1+a_N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $a_N$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $a_{20}=66,$ $N=20,$ and $S_N=560$ into the formula above and solving for $a_1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}560 & =\\frac{20}{2}({a}_{1}+66) \\\\ 560 & =10({a}_{1}+66) \\\\ \\frac{560}{10} & ={a}_{1}+66 \\\\ 56 & ={a}_{1}+66 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078224 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Common Difference and the Sum"}] :question/id #uuid "9e118fb4-4787-5ed1-9ab9-13cfce102726" :question/math-academy-id "e-4207" :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=2,$ and the sum of the first $50$ terms is $S_{50}=2\\,150?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}\\big( 2a_1+(N-1)d \\big),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=50,$ $d=2,$ and $S_N=2\\,150$ into the formula above and solving for $a_1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\,150 & =\\frac{50}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(50-1)(2)) \\\\ 4\\,300 & =50(2{a}_{1}+98) \\\\ \\frac{4\\,300}{50} & =2{a}_{1}+98 \\\\ 86 & =2{a}_{1}+98 \\\\ -12 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078225 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given a Term and the Sum"}] :question/id #uuid "4de8d7af-50a7-5e9d-8f5d-908d6a06e174" :question/math-academy-id "e-4208" :question/problem "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $11$th term is $29$ and the sum of the first $16$ terms of the series is $384.$" :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}\\left( 2a_1+(N-1)d \\right),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N = 16$ and $S_N = 384$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 384 & =\\frac{16}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(16-1)d) \\\\ 384 & =8(2{a}_{1}+15d) \\\\ \\frac{384}{8} & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ 48 & =2{a}_{1}+15d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $11$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{11} & ={a}_{1}+(11-1)d \\\\ 29 & ={a}_{1}+10d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}29={a}_{1}+10d \\\\ 48=2{a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-58 & =-2{a}_{1}-20d \\\\ 48 & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -10 & =-5d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d = 2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & ={a}_{1}+10(2) \\\\ 29 & ={a}_{1}+20 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d7a21aa-f2e3-5461-81a6-5cbd0f63c03d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Last Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d338226d-f8cc-5e25-89fa-c694992e2851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319679} {:answer/id #uuid "18df0d97-5148-549f-8338-2a5221ff0cda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319680} {:answer/id #uuid "7e647899-3041-58c5-b0a4-d1e8034f6b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319681} {:answer/id #uuid "4a5f8270-dd21-5c45-a6b5-76a9386ee0f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319682} {:answer/id #uuid "1566f176-db34-5dcd-8a13-c7087a83f337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1566f176-db34-5dcd-8a13-c7087a83f337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319683} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f81c458-0d06-5212-ad1a-e7f274a27475" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb7cdbfc-1760-5ad3-b63a-5d852476871b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108630" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $36$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{36}=\\frac{225}{2},$ and the last term is ${a}_{36}=\\frac{11}{2},$ what is the first term of the series?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{36}=\\frac{11}{2}$, $N=36$, and ${S}_{N}=\\frac{225}{2}$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{225}{2} & =\\frac{36}{2}({a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{225}{36} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ \\frac{25}{4} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{25}{4}-\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given a Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ae6a22c-8d11-56c2-9596-d174a31c2231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319686} {:answer/id #uuid "5bac4b7d-1f57-5b55-82d6-af462dc60784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319687} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0fb856-acd1-5082-b7f3-6d9e0d0bc587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319688} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb6df4f-c778-5ae1-b175-ce811f2b470c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319689} {:answer/id #uuid "2b61e236-ca99-58e9-bd83-db330903c91e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bac4b7d-1f57-5b55-82d6-af462dc60784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319687} :answer-field/id #uuid "1eb10240-d1f1-5001-949d-bced3721068b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "60e9a618-f20a-5ccf-9c10-25260f7c4404" :question/math-academy-id "q-108724" :question/problem "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $5$th term is $-0.28$ and the sum of the first $12$ terms of the series is $-12.$" :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=12$ and ${S}_{N}=-12$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{12}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(12-1)d) \\\\ -12 & =6(2{a}_{1}+11d) \\\\ -2 & =2{a}_{1}+11d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $5$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}+(5-1)d \\\\ -0.28 & ={a}_{1}+4d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-0.28={a}_{1}+4d \\\\ -2=2{a}_{1}+11d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.56 & =-2{a}_{1}-8d \\\\ -2 & =2{a}_{1}+11d \\\\ -1.44 & =3d \\\\ d & =-0.48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-0.48$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-0.28 & ={a}_{1}+4(-0.48) \\\\ -0.28 & ={a}_{1}-1.92 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.64.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d7a21aa-f2e3-5461-81a6-5cbd0f63c03d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Last Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f84a4da1-19dc-5ad4-8354-348f750971a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232843} {:answer/id #uuid "502c605e-4428-5a1d-b76e-3c9c0467ba38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f84a4da1-19dc-5ad4-8354-348f750971a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232843} :answer-field/id #uuid "b09624b5-b584-5ff3-89f8-3e364ab73158" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "895e7cfd-35af-5059-ba6b-4107204ac08f" :question/math-academy-id "q-233787" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $50$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{50}=600,$ and the last term is ${a}_{50}=21.8,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{50}=21.8$, $N=50$, and ${S}_{N}=600$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}600 & =\\frac{50}{2}({a}_{1}+21.8) \\\\ 600 & =25({a}_{1}+21.8) \\\\ \\frac{600}{25} & ={a}_{1}+21.8 \\\\ 24 & ={a}_{1}+21.8 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Common Difference and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f9dcafe-d6f6-5fff-897d-d70c4ed4d07f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f9dcafe-d6f6-5fff-897d-d70c4ed4d07f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319694} :answer-field/id #uuid "f98866ee-ac4e-5beb-a49b-75832a45d69b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05161e8f-e95d-5bde-9b69-96629df57e04" :question/math-academy-id "q-233995" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $29$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{29}=319,$ and the common difference is $d=-3,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=29$, $d=-3$, and ${S}_{N}=319$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}319 & =\\frac{29}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(29-1)(-3)) \\\\ 638 & =29(2{a}_{1}-84) \\\\ 22 & =2{a}_{1}-84 \\\\ 106 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =53.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given a Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab0cc772-bbe7-5a4c-8513-7cadd3009f2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232844} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1ac7ad-3077-5894-809d-9a4624a97ca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab0cc772-bbe7-5a4c-8513-7cadd3009f2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232844} :answer-field/id #uuid "31e7d317-69c1-55b7-ab7a-309b9d135553" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c91fb15c-96e5-5371-8c4b-2038c367ea64" :question/math-academy-id "q-233997" :question/problem "If the $15$th term of an arithmetic series is $-53$ and the sum of the first $21$ terms is $-777,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=21$ and ${S}_{N}=-777$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -777 & =\\frac{21}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(21-1)d) \\\\ -1\\,554= & 21(2{a}_{1}+20d) \\\\ -74 & =2{a}_{1}+20d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $15$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{15} & ={a}_{1}+(15-1)d \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}+14d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-53={a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -74=2{a}_{1}+20d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}106 & =-2{a}_{1}-28d \\\\ -74 & =2{a}_{1}+20d \\\\ 32 & =-8d \\\\ d & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-4$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-53 & ={a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}+14(-4) \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}-56 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d7a21aa-f2e3-5461-81a6-5cbd0f63c03d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Last Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f741519-dbc1-5f4f-81f9-6647f7131564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f741519-dbc1-5f4f-81f9-6647f7131564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319698} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bdb5469-bd87-5679-894a-ce2f07603eb7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319697}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3f57bb6-e095-5580-af3c-db798c84b3e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-250824" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{20}=-635,$ and the last term is ${a}_{20}=-65,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{20}=-65$, $N=20$, and ${S}_{N}=-635$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-635 & =\\frac{20}{2}({a}_{1}+(-65)) \\\\ -635 & =10({a}_{1}-65) \\\\ -\\frac{635}{10} & ={a}_{1}-65 \\\\ -63.5 & ={a}_{1}-65 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d7a21aa-f2e3-5461-81a6-5cbd0f63c03d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Last Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c98d7d76-9213-5bfd-9865-88dc75073ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c98d7d76-9213-5bfd-9865-88dc75073ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319701} :answer-field/id #uuid "fde673a7-82df-57c0-97af-b737b43935a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ec12e89-df49-505f-87f0-09e7f188d155" :question/math-academy-id "q-250826" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $32$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{32}=648,$ and the last term is ${a}_{32}=37.3,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{32}=37.3$, $N=32$, and ${S}_{N}=648$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}648 & =\\frac{32}{2}({a}_{1}+37.3) \\\\ 648 & =16({a}_{1}+37.3) \\\\ \\frac{648}{16} & ={a}_{1}+37.3 \\\\ 40.5 & ={a}_{1}+37.3 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Common Difference and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b96b99e-5c2c-5c3c-917c-eff2002dd3e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b96b99e-5c2c-5c3c-917c-eff2002dd3e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319704} :answer-field/id #uuid "e24fdcde-54c5-50a2-a9cd-743d36dd1602" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40ae85a2-da7c-5fcc-8fba-db8deb8365ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-250834" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $36$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{36}=2\\,142,$ and the common difference is $d=3,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=36$, $d=3$, and ${S}_{N}=2\\,142$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\,142 & =\\frac{36}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(36-1)(3)) \\\\ 2\\,142 & =18(2{a}_{1}+105) \\\\ 119 & =2{a}_{1}+105 \\\\ 14 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Common Difference and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa5256c7-acbd-58f1-92d5-ade9cf7d73da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232866} {:answer/id #uuid "93326fab-65bb-5b4e-9d6b-5b7ca3c19f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa5256c7-acbd-58f1-92d5-ade9cf7d73da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232866} :answer-field/id #uuid "60fad5f1-dce6-5c63-8880-7b180156a9ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69029c1f-f66a-5123-9c29-926f5d8155d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-250844" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{20}=301,$ and the common difference is $d=1.5,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$, $d=1.5$, and ${S}_{N}=301$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}301 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)(1.5)) \\\\ 301 & =10(2{a}_{1}+28.5) \\\\ 30.1 & =2{a}_{1}+28.5 \\\\ 1.6 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given a Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc5503ee-1b46-5288-b69d-63e1a8800d95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319708} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d7afa3-bd90-5a65-8996-bc2a5a545bda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc5503ee-1b46-5288-b69d-63e1a8800d95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319708} :answer-field/id #uuid "17cd7f1e-32a6-52ac-a9c7-4007ea2c9e45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a22c14f9-3812-5d88-ba4b-6e25ffa53a6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-250863" :question/problem "If the $16$th term of an arithmetic series is $-32$ and the sum of the first $20$ terms is $-200,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$ and ${S}_{N}=-200$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -200 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)d) \\\\ -200 & =10(2{a}_{1}+19d) \\\\ -20 & =2{a}_{1}+19d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $16$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{16} & ={a}_{1}+(16-1)d \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-32={a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -20=2{a}_{1}+19d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64 & =-2{a}_{1}-30d \\\\ -20 & =2{a}_{1}+19d \\\\ 44 & =-11d \\\\ d & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-4$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-32 & ={a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}+15(-4) \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}-60 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given a Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae3d69e5-d4d7-5a0c-887b-877ab32d5b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae3d69e5-d4d7-5a0c-887b-877ab32d5b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319712} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae44cffe-4ac1-54af-8af0-6bb954e5528b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "071ccade-a6f8-5e6b-af5a-bbbc446621b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-250878" :question/problem "If the $9$th term of an arithmetic series is $\\frac{46}{3}$ and the sum of the first $15$ terms is $200,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=15$ and ${S}_{N}=200$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 200 & =\\frac{15}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(15-1)d) \\\\ 400 & =15(2{a}_{1}+14d) \\\\ \\frac{400}{15} & =2{a}_{1}+14d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3} & =2{a}_{1}+14d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $9$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{9} & ={a}_{1}+(9-1)d \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{46}{3}={a}_{1}+8d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3}=2{a}_{1}+14d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{92}{3} & =-2{a}_{1}-16d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3} & =2{a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -\\frac{12}{3} & =-2d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8d \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8(2) \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+16 \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{48}{3} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given a Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42476e40-c10c-542c-a508-59f13940c25e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42476e40-c10c-542c-a508-59f13940c25e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319715} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df3aa0a-3535-5e13-9c81-f69f91a522a0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f12cd0e2-1bab-50a8-952e-2186b606facf" :question/math-academy-id "q-250881" :question/problem "If the $6$th term of an arithmetic series is $\\frac{37}{4}$ and the sum of the first $16$ terms is $228,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=16$ and ${S}_{N}=228$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 228 & =\\frac{16}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(16-1)d) \\\\ 228 & =8(2{a}_{1}+15d) \\\\ \\frac{57}{2} & =2{a}_{1}+15d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $6$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}+(6-1)d \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37}{4}={a}_{1}+5d \\\\ \\frac{57}{2}=2{a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{37}{2} & =-2{a}_{1}-10d \\\\ \\frac{57}{2} & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ \\frac{20}{2} & =5d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5d \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5(2) \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{40}{4} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d7a21aa-f2e3-5461-81a6-5cbd0f63c03d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Last Term and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc51035-39d3-5111-a061-73661262e858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319718} {:answer/id #uuid "058ac5e9-a3b0-57a7-9947-8f75c5860bc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319719} {:answer/id #uuid "9677e06b-492e-5e23-ba7e-a8dc19178635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319720} {:answer/id #uuid "c45afdd0-3c31-5583-918b-e9b31d57cc5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319721} {:answer/id #uuid "d83d2b50-1044-5487-8647-771564f12f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83d2b50-1044-5487-8647-771564f12f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319722} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc370fae-9bad-56e2-86de-bce6a23c2576" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93078165-4628-5085-9eb3-223554735697" :question/math-academy-id "q-39255" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $18$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{18}=-495,$ and the last term is ${a}_{18}=-62,$ what is the first term of the series?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{18}=-62$, $N=18$, and ${S}_{N}=-495$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-495 & =\\frac{18}{2}({a}_{1}-62) \\\\ -495 & =9({a}_{1}-62) \\\\ \\frac{-495}{9} & ={a}_{1}-62 \\\\ -55 & ={a}_{1}-62 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Common Difference and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8839e968-3031-5d36-a10d-22d30998292c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "134" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077470} {:answer/id #uuid "e42008e1-3800-5829-acbb-80cc4dcb4f37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077471} {:answer/id #uuid "04f22df6-5364-5676-bc31-3e62dff60848" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077472} {:answer/id #uuid "41866c46-b73b-573a-91ee-940642ade2db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077473} {:answer/id #uuid "4af99001-a697-50d5-b2f7-315b66fd6f69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e42008e1-3800-5829-acbb-80cc4dcb4f37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077471} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce8d4817-d1f2-5124-aa74-b063bccc9d4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84620f29-83f0-5dfe-aa1e-c9ccf5d9b8e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-5602" :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=-4,$ and the sum of the first $20$ terms is ${S}_{20}=1\\,160?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$, $d=-4$, and ${S}_{N}=1\\,160$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,160 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)(-4)) \\\\ 1\\,160 & =10(2{a}_{1}-76) \\\\ 116 & =2{a}_{1}-76 \\\\ 192 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =96.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Common Difference and the Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb9e6e4f-e13a-5e20-99b8-27ed9a2a226f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319725} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc4492d-3a6e-52bd-b687-cc15fc952020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319726} {:answer/id #uuid "503cb077-2fbf-5c64-9a34-6f2d65b850eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319727} {:answer/id #uuid "0563f152-9438-5b48-be28-77ee44255457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319728} {:answer/id #uuid "4341e96a-7131-5460-a29b-3e611b827de5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0563f152-9438-5b48-be28-77ee44255457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319728} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f2af7f5-a188-51ce-903f-fb5fc7816a04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "986217a9-c189-528a-b6af-7efab665859e" :question/math-academy-id "q-5606" :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=-2,$ and the sum of the first $20$ terms is ${S}_{20}=-160?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$, $d=-2$, and ${S}_{N}=-160$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-160 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)(-2)) \\\\ -160 & =10(2{a}_{1}-38) \\\\ -16 & =2{a}_{1}-38 \\\\ 22 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
